{"name":"Archaeology","hex":"#6e6a5e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"archaeology","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The study of the past by excavation and analysis of its material remains.\n\nThe actual excavation, examination, analysis, and interpretation.","The actual excavation, examination, analysis, and interpretation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/archaeology"}],"entries":[{"title":"Archaeology","blocks":[{"text":"Archaeology or archeology is the study of human activity through the recovery and analysis of material culture. The archaeological record consists of artifacts, architecture, biofacts or ecofacts, sites, and cultural landscapes. Archaeology can be considered both a social science and a branch of the humanities. It is usually considered an independent academic discipline, but may also be classified as part of anthropology, history or geography. The discipline involves surveying, excavation, and eventually analysis of data collected, to learn more about the past. In broad scope, archaeology relies on cross-disciplinary research."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Dolina-Pano-3_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Dolina-Pano-3_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archaeology","wikidata":"Q23498"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Nabonidus_cylinder_sippar_bm1.jpg/500px-Nabonidus_cylinder_sippar_bm1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Nabonidus_cylinder_sippar_bm1.jpg/500px-Nabonidus_cylinder_sippar_bm1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANabonidus_cylinder_sippar_bm1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Nabonidus